Ayzrian probably is offering to make state type generic that extends object. Here is the current interface for SceneContext:

`export interface SceneContext<TContext extends SceneContextMessageUpdate> {
  ctx: TContext;

  scenes: Map<string, Scene<TContext>>;

  options: SceneContextOptions;

  readonly session: {
    state?: object,
    current?: string,
    expires?: number
  },

  **state: object;   // Make thip type generic extending object**

  readonly current: BaseScene<TContext> | null;

  reset: () => void;

  enter: (sceneId: string, initialState?: object, silent?: boolean) => Promise<any>;

  reenter: () => Promise<any>;

  leave: () => Promise<any>
}`

Ayzrian as a workaround you can use typecasting too.

`interface MyScene {
    name: string
}

let sceneState = ctx.scene.state as MyScene
sceneState.name = "Nazar" // You would have autocomplete and no typescript error warnings.
`

I also have the same problem.
I am trying to use Scene's state, but it's not possible because it's typed as an `object`.
See the typing:
```ts
export interface SceneContext<TContext extends SceneContextMessageUpdate> {
  ctx: TContext;

  scenes: Map<string, Scene<TContext>>;

  options: SceneContextOptions;

  readonly session: {
    state?: object,
    current?: string,
    expires?: number
  },

  state: object;

  readonly current: BaseScene<TContext> | null;

  reset: () => void;

  enter: (sceneId: string, initialState?: object, silent?: boolean) => Promise<any>;

  reenter: () => Promise<any>;

  leave: () => Promise<any>
}
```
`state` here is an object.
I would resolve this by creating a setting the `state` property to an interface so developers can extend the SceneState object with their own definitions.

Faced with the same issue but figured out a trick.

**tsconfig.json**
```ts
"typeRoots": ["./node_modules/@types", "./src/@types"] 
```

**custom.d.ts**
```ts
import {WizardContextWizard, WizardSessionData} from "telegraf/typings/scenes";
import {CastProperty} from "../utils/utility-types.util";
import Context from "telegraf/typings/context";
import SceneContextScene from "telegraf/typings/scenes/context";
import {WizardSession} from "telegraf/typings/scenes/wizard/context";

namespace Scenes {
	interface WizardContext<S extends object = any, D extends WizardSessionData = WizardSessionData> extends Context {
		session: WizardSession<D>;
		scene: SceneContextScene<WizardContext<D>, D>;
		wizard: CastProperty<WizardContextWizard<WizardContext<D>>, "state", S>;
	}
}
```

**cast-property**
```ts
export type CastProperty<SOURCE, PROPERTY, TYPE> = {
	[K in keyof SOURCE]: K extends PROPERTY ? TYPE : SOURCE[K];
};
```

**usage**
```ts
import {Scenes} from "telegraf";

const doSomething = (context: Scenes.WizardContext<{someProp: string}>) => {
	console.log(context.wizard.state.someProp);
}
```

